# Avatar

> Lede 0.7.0's docs for Avatar, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/avatar.md

An `<img>` with alt text, or initials on a tint when there's no picture or it fails to load.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/avatar
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md) and [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md). The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.0/avatar.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { Avatar } from '@/components/lede/avatar';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/avatar.tsx` | `@/components/lede/avatar` | `Avatar` (component), `AvatarProps` (type) |

## Props

A real `<img>` with alt text when there's a picture, and initials on a tint when there isn't. Other HTML attributes and `ref` go on whichever of the two renders, so the ref's element changes when the image fails. `loading`, `decoding`, `referrerPolicy` and `crossOrigin` go on the `<img>` alone.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `name` (required) | `string` |  | Whose avatar this is: the source of the initials and, unless `alt` is set, the text alternative. |
| `src` | `string` |  | Picture URL. With none, or if it fails to load, the initials show. |
| `alt` | `string` | `name` | Text alternative. Default `name`. Pass `""` when the name is already beside the avatar, so it isn't read twice. |
| `size` | `'md' \| 'lg'` | `md` | `'md'` fits ListRow's leading slot, and `'lg'` leads a profile. Default `'md'`. |
| `ref` | `React.Ref<HTMLImageElement \| HTMLSpanElement>` |  | The `<img>`, or the `<span>` of initials. It changes from one to the other when the image fails to load. |

Avatar also takes HTML attributes, such as `className`, and the `loading`, `decoding`, `referrerPolicy` and `crossOrigin` attributes of `<img>`.

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { Avatar } from '@/components/lede/avatar';

export function Author({ name, picture }: { name: string; picture?: string }) {
  return (
    <p>
      {/* The name is beside it, so the picture's alt is empty. */}
      <Avatar name={name} src={picture} alt="" /> {name}
    </p>
  );
}
```

Docs: [Components](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/components.md).

